From 51b4109e5dfab268ebefcbacac7b4e2968b1f367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:52:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] MAINTAINERS: add the HiSilicon STB clock driver entry

The Hi3798MV100 CRG clock driver has no maintainer entry. The driver is
a DT-binding driver reviewed under linux-clk.

Register the driver with its binding and clock headers.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
---
 MAINTAINERS | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/MAINTAINERS
+++ b/MAINTAINERS
@@ -12202,6 +12202,15 @@ S:	Maintained
 F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/hisilicon,hi6421-spmi-pmic.yaml
 F:	drivers/mfd/hi6421-spmi-pmic.c
 
+HISILICON STB CLOCK DRIVER
+M:	David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
+L:	linux-clk@vger.kernel.org
+L:	linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
+S:	Maintained
+F:	Documentation/devicetree/bindings/clock/hisilicon,hisi-crg.yaml
+F:	drivers/clk/hisilicon/crg-hi3798mv100.c
+F:	include/dt-bindings/clock/hisilicon,hi3798mv100-*.h
+
 HISILICON STB VOLTAGE REGULATOR DRIVER
 M:	David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 L:	linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org
